# Narration v3 passages (51), one generation each, lines separated by newlines. Verbatim from the final storyboard.
# (passage id, first position, last position, [lines])
PASSAGES = [
("P01",1,2,["You became the #1 streamer overnight.","Yesterday, you streamed to almost nobody."]),
("P02",3,5,["You talked to an empty room — and you kept talking anyway.","This morning, your phone will not stop buzzing.","You sit down in the same chair, in the same small room."]),
("P03",6,7,["You press one button.","The red light turns on.","And the room explodes.","The chat is moving so fast you cannot read one single name."]),
("P04",8,8,["Ten thousand people are watching.","Then it climbs to fifty thousand viewers.","Now you have surpassed one hundred thousand people watching — and the viewers are still climbing."]),
("P05",9,10,["Someone gifts you one hundred subscribers.","Moments later you get gifted a thousand subscribers.","Your name is on every phone, on every screen, and all over social media."]),
("P06",11,12,["Your friends are texting you — you did it. You actually did it.","You are just someone sitting in a small room, watching your whole life change on a screen."]),
("P07",13,14,["And tonight, you are going to do something no streamer in history has ever done.","You are going to cross one million subscribers."]),
("P08",15,16,["But before we go any further","There are three hidden truths about that chair nobody tells you.","And the third one is why nobody keeps that chair forever."]),
("P09",17,18,["Let's take a look at what actually just happened to you last night.","There are more than six million people who have pressed that same button you pressed.","Six million."]),
("P10",19,20,["Most of them stream to an empty room — the same empty room you streamed to yesterday.","Out of all six million, only about eighty thousand become an official partner."]),
("P11",21,22,["And above all of them, there is one chair.","This morning, that chair became yours."]),
("P12",23,23,["Before you sat in that chair this morning","A handful of streamers have sat there before you."]),
("P13",24,24,["In 2018 Ninja was the biggest streamer in the world during the peak of Fortnite. Every platform fought over him and he held the title for years."]),
("P14",25,25,["Ludwig took Ninja's throne in 2021 — he did a subathon and went live for a month straight without stopping. By the end of the subathon he had surpassed Ninja and became the #1 streamer in the world."]),
("P15",26,26,["But Kai Cenat holds the record itself — he achieved over a million subscribers in 2025 during his subathon, more than anyone in history."]),
("P16",27,28,["Three different men. Three different runs at the same chair.","And every one of them learned something about that chair — something nobody can really teach you until you are already sitting in the chair.","What they learned is the first hidden truth."]),
("P17",29,30,["Which is the truth about the money.","Every single name on that counter is a subscription that pays about six dollars a month.","Six dollars sounds like nothing.","It is the price of a coffee."]),
("P18",31,32,["But tonight, you are going to surpass one million subscribers.","Now — that $6 is gross. The website takes its cut first.","About half of every subscription goes to the platform before it ever reaches you."]),
("P19",33,33,["And still.","The last time a streamer made a run like yours, they grossed an estimate in subscriber money alone at about three and a half million dollars.","In one month."]),
("P20",34,34,["And he had fewer subscribers than you are about to have.","That is just the subscribers."]),
("P21",35,36,["You haven't even realized what else is in store for you.","Because once a crowd that size exists, the companies come next.","One streamer showed his real numbers for one month. His name is Ludwig."]),
("P22",37,38,["His viewers and his streaming sites paid him over three hundred thousand dollars — but the brands paid him eight hundred thousand dollars.","The companies that want to stand next to your crowd pay more than the crowd does."]),
("P23",39,40,["And then there are the platforms themselves — the websites fighting to be the place you stream.","One platform, called Mixer, reportedly paid Ninja between twenty and thirty million dollars."]),
("P24",41,42,["Just to stream on their site instead of Twitch.","So add it up.","Millions from the subscribers climbing on your screen."]),
("P25",43,45,["Hundreds of thousands from the brands lining up behind them.","Tens of millions from the platforms fighting over you.","That is truth number one.","The money does not come from one place.","It comes from everywhere — all at the same time."]),
("P26",46,46,["Now let's uncover the hidden truth number 2.","Truth number two is about power."]),
("P27",47,47,["Yesterday, you wrote to people — and nobody wrote back.","You asked brands to notice you. Nothing.","You asked the platforms for a chance. Silence."]),
("P28",48,49,["Today, everybody answers in minutes.","The platforms are not just paying you. They are calling you.","Each one wants you standing on their side.","And they are not calling because of how you play.","They are calling because of the crowd standing behind you."]),
("P29",50,51,["Because that is what you own now.","A crowd that companies cannot build for themselves — so they have to come to you.","The famous names you used to watch?","They are asking to come on YOUR stream now."]),
("P30",52,53,["Not because you are famous like them.","Because your room is where the people are — and being seen in your room is worth money to them.","And your crowd is not just an audience anymore.","It is a store, a TV channel, and a billboard — all in one place."]),
("P31",54,55,["You point at a product, and it sells out.","You point at a tiny streamer nobody knows — a kid in a small room, talking to nobody, just like you were yesterday — and his room explodes in seconds."]),
("P32",56,57,["You can make somebody else's whole business change in one night.","With one sentence.","Yesterday, you needed the world","Today, the world needs you."]),
("P33",58,59,["And it knocks on your door — politely.","This leads you now to the final hidden truth.","But."]),
("P34",60,60,["In this final hidden truth there lies a catch.","And the catch is this: becoming the #1 streamer overnight was only half the battle."]),
("P35",61,62,["Staying as the #1 streamer is just as hard — maybe harder.","Because your chair does not just stay yours.","The moment you stop, you start falling."]),
("P36",63,64,["Ninja once took two days off while being the #1 streamer in the world.","In those two days he lost forty thousand subscribers.","Two days off is all it took."]),
("P37",65,66,["So today you go live. And tomorrow. And the next day.","There is no day off at number one.","There is only live — or falling."]),
("P38",67,68,["And remember the six million people pressing that same button?","They all want your chair.","The record you are about to set tonight has been taken before — and taken back.","Somebody is always coming for it."]),
("P39",69,69,["And here is the biggest catch of this whole video.","The part nobody told you and the last thing you are thinking about at this current moment.","Majority of the millions of subscribers you just got… were gifts."]),
("P40",70,71,["And that gifted subscriber comes with an expiration date.","The gift only lasts one month.","Then it is gone — unless that person reaches into their own pocket and pays again.","Most of them do not."]),
("P41",72,73,["It already happened to Kai Cenat — the man who held this record before you.","He crossed a million subscribers — the first in history.","A few weeks later, he looked at his number.","About forty thousand were left.","More than nine out of ten — gone."]),
("P42",74,75,["Not because he failed.","Because the calendar said so.","And look at what Kai Cenat did exactly just to win those one million subscribers."]),
("P43",76,77,["He streamed for thirty days straight. Twenty-four hours a day.","He slept on camera. He lived on camera.","One whole month of his life — dedicated to keeping the crown he already won.","That is what it might take for you to stay at the top."]),
("P44",78,78,["Your customers cancel themselves.","Every thirty days.","So how do you win it back?"]),
("P45",79,80,["You continue to stream.","Every single day.","No days off.","And that is why getting to the throne of #1 is only half the battle."]),
("P46",81,82,["The crown is not a prize you get to keep.","It is a bill that comes due every thirty days.","And there are millions of people coming for that throne of yours.","Who will do whatever it takes to get there."]),
("P47",83,84,["You got there overnight.","You went to sleep as nobody.","And you woke up as the biggest show on Earth."]),
("P48",85,86,["The money is real.","Millions from the subscribers.","Even more from the brands standing behind them.","And possibly tens of millions from the platforms fighting to hold you."]),
("P49",87,87,["The power is real too.","Yesterday, you needed the world","Today, the world needs you."]),
("P50",88,89,["But your crown runs on a thirty-day clock.","Your subscribers expire.","A couple days off can cost you everything."]),
("P51",90,91,["And six million streamers are pressing that same button, coming for your chair.","That is the business of being number one.","You became the #1 streamer overnight.","Staying at #1 is just as hard."]),
]
